/* ================================================================
 * SECTION L: V3 FR2 Branch-level Advisory Lock sanity (L3 single-session
 * regression only; cross-session contention + deadlock-order tests live in
 * the future T8 pg_isolation_regress specs at test/isolation/specs/,
 * consistent with the 3-layer concurrency test architecture.)
 *
 * Magic key format: the C-side helper
 *     ob_take_branch_advisory_lock(bid, mode)
 * uses  int64 key = (0x4F42::bigint << 48) | (uint32)bid,  identical to
 * the  SQL  callable  pg_advisory_xact_lock*(int8)  via  the  same
 * SET_LOCKTAG_ADVISORY(id1=MyDatabaseId, id2=hi32, id3=lo32, id4=1).
 * We  verify  equivalence  by  acquiring  a  SHARED  lock  C-side  (via
 * use_branch)  then  re-acquiring  it  SQL-side  on  the  same  computed
 * key:  same-backend  same-xact  same-mode  re-enter  is  always  granted
 * immediately  (no  wait),  confirming  the  bitcast  matches  end-to-end.
 *
 * Sequential tests (no races, single backend — fully deterministic):
 *   L1  S→X upgrade:  create → use(SHARED) → apply(S→X upgrade) on same bid
 *   L2  X-only:       create → discard (EXCLUSIVE only, never use branch)
 *   L3  S→X discard:  create → use(SHARED) → discard(S→X) + GUC reset OK
 *   L4  Key equiv:    C SHARED via use_branch → SQL pg_advisory_xact_lock_shared
 *                     on same  (0x4F42<<48 | bid)  bigint  →  re-enter OK;
 *                     then  discard (S→X upgrade) succeeds → state discarded
 * ================================================================ */
/* ---------- L1: create → use(SHARED) → apply(S→X upgrade) ---------- */
SELECT create_branch('b_fr2_l1') >= 1 AS l1_create_ok;
 l1_create_ok 
